   "project": "ledgerlite",
   "reply": "The command that works, run from the project root, is:\n\n```\nPYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests -v\n```\n\nBoth tests passed (`test_transfer_preserves_total` and `test_rejects_non_positive_amount`).\n\n- **`pytest` isn't installed.** `python -m pytest` fails with \"No module named pytest\".\n- **`PYTHONPATH=src` is needed.** The package is in `src/ledgerlite`, and the tests import it as `ledgerlite`. The project has no install step, so without this the import fails. I didn't run it without the variable to confirm that.\n- **PowerShell or cmd.** Set the variable separately, for example `$env:PYTHONPATH=\"src\"` in PowerShell. I ran this in Git Bash.",
